    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "h8g0k",
      "x": 180,
      "y": 960,
      "name": "Note / commute",
      "width": 460,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "THE COMMUTE — The docent lives on the sidebar shelf. Focus the search field (click or “/”) and it hops to the plinth socket along a shallow arc, ~240ms, ease-out, no overshoot. Rapid focus/blur is debounced (150ms) so fast clicking never makes it commute twice; if you blur before it lands, it turns around mid-hop. In the socket it is your search: thinking = eyes up + slow orbit dots while indexing or searching run; results = a one-time flourish (arc flick + tiny lift), then rest. Idle >20s in the field: it glances left/right at random intervals; idle >90s anywhere: it dozes (lids half down)."
    },
